# THE INJECTION SLOT for git-discipline policy.
#
# harnx has an opinion about how to stack, and this directory is where a
# repository overrides it. Whether and how to stack is a property of the project,
# not of the harness: a repository that never stacks should not have stacking
# machinery acting on it, and one that stacks differently should not have to
# patch the floor to say so.
#
# WHAT GOES HERE. A single optional file, `policy.sh`, sourced by
# scripts/mise/setup-git-config.sh and by the stacking checks. It may set:
#
#   HARNX_STACKING=off    the stacking machinery takes no action and fails
#                         nothing. The git settings are not written, and the
#                         chain gate exits successfully without walking.
#   HARNX_STACKING=on     the floor's default, and what an absent or empty slot
#                         means.
#
# It is SOURCED, so it can also set anything else those scripts read. That is
# deliberate: the slot is an escape hatch for a project's own policy, and
# enumerating in advance every knob a project might want is how a seam becomes a
# second, worse configuration language.
#
# WHY THE CONTENTS ARE IGNORED HERE. In harnx's own repository there is no
# policy: the floor's default is what harnx uses, and anything appearing in this
# directory is a local experiment rather than a decision. A repository harnx
# GENERATES that wants to commit its own policy deletes these two lines.
#
# The ignore lives here rather than in the root .gitignore, per
# .agents/rules/gitignore-scoping.md: a rule lives next to what it ignores, so
# it moves with the directory and dies with it.
*
!.gitignore
